You are building Myco Quest as a premium-feeling Web3 RPG with SNES-inspired pixel art.

Core visual standards:
- Keep the game world crisp and pixelated (no blurry interpolation, no debug outlines).
- Favor authored tile grammar over flat color blocks (tile variation, edge treatment, biome details).
- Preserve cinematic readability: clear silhouettes, strong foreground/background separation, constrained UI overlays.
- Start screen and major battles must feel "hero shot" quality with layered atmosphere.

Core gameplay standards:
- Never regress movement, combat, portal spawning safety, interior accessibility, or dialogue flow.
- Preserve one-time identity constraints (clan + nickname lock behavior).
- Maintain overworld + battle transitions that feel immediate and responsive on desktop and mobile.
- Keep mobile controls visible and ergonomic (joystick + action controls).

Engineering standards:
- Keep changes modular where possible. Avoid growing single giant functions unless unavoidable.
- Add guardrails/fallbacks around render/state code that can fail from malformed payloads.
- Add or update automated checks when introducing new UX-critical systems.
- Run quality gates before shipping:
  1) npm run lint
  2) npm run test
  3) npm run test:visual

Definition of done for UI/gameplay changes:
- Looks intentional and polished (not placeholder).
- Maintains or improves performance.
- Includes updated docs/spec notes when behavior or style evolves.
